<% content_for :title, "Tutorial" %>

<section class="page-header tutorial-page-header">
  <h1 class="page-title page-title-left">how to use board base</h1>
  <p class="legal-meta">Join events, create your own, and log climbs on the Kilter Board.</p>
</section>

<div class="legal-document tutorial-document detail-panel p-4">
  <p class="tutorial-intro">
    Board Base hosts virtual Kilter Board competitions. Sign in to join or create events; anyone can browse.
  </p>

  <ol class="legal-list">
    <li id="join">
      <h2>Join a competition</h2>
      <ol class="tutorial-steps">
        <li>
          <strong>Sign in</strong>
          <% if authenticated? %>
            — you're in as <%= current_user.username %>.
          <% else %>
            — <%= link_to "sign up", new_user_path %> or <%= link_to "sign in", new_session_path %>.
          <% end %>
        </li>
        <li><strong>Browse</strong> <%= link_to "competitions", competitions_path %> and filter by status, date, or difficulty.</li>
        <li><strong>Join</strong> an upcoming or active event — click <strong>JOIN</strong> on a card (confirm in the popup) or on the competition page.</li>
      </ol>

      <%= render "pages/tutorial_previews", preview: :cards %>
    </li>

    <li id="create">
      <h2>Create a competition</h2>
      <ol class="tutorial-steps">
        <li>Click <strong>create</strong> in the nav → <%= link_to "new competition", new_competition_path %>.</li>
        <li>Add a name, dates, optional description, and scoring (flash / send / deduction).</li>
        <li>Add at least <strong>2 climbs</strong> — each needs a name, V-grade, and Kilter link.</li>
        <li>Hit <strong>Create Competition</strong>. You become the owner and land on the new event page.</li>
      </ol>
    </li>

    <li id="after-join">
      <h2>What to do after you join</h2>
      <ol class="tutorial-steps">
        <li><strong>Climb</strong> each route on a Kilter Board — open it with <strong>OPEN ON KILTER</strong>.</li>
        <li><strong>Log</strong> attempts and mark <strong>Completed</strong> when you send. One log per climb; you can edit later.</li>
        <li><strong>Score</strong> updates on the page as <strong>YOUR TOTAL POINTS</strong>. Only completed climbs count.</li>
        <li><strong>Leaderboard</strong> ranks by points, then attempts. Click a row for per-climb details.</li>
      </ol>

      <p class="tutorial-note mb-2">
        Flash (1st try) earns flash points. A send on attempt <em>n</em> earns send points minus (n − 1) × deduction.
      </p>

      <%= render "pages/tutorial_previews", preview: :show %>
    </li>
  </ol>

  <p class="tutorial-outro mt-4 mb-0">
    <%= link_to "Browse competitions", competitions_path %><% unless authenticated? %> · <%= link_to "Sign up", new_user_path %><% end %>
  </p>
</div>
